// The transport pack of this emit target (transport_serialization_design.md §6.0): which wire
// protocol tags and carrier tags this compiler build provides. The language's vocabulary is the
// union of every target's pack; a program that names a tag this pack does not list is rejected by
// sir_target_verify with E2410 before anything is emitted. Every emit target carries its own copy
// at emitter/<TARGET>/transport_pack.silica, read by the shared compiler like pack_descriptions.
// The board's transport set is decided per board release (design §6.0, §6.4). This release provides
// ETF: the wire protocol is pure Silica (compiler/stdlib/wire_etf.silica) over the transport builtins,
// which the emitter lowers (terms/prims/prims_transport.silica) onto the board runtime's
// rt_transport.S; only the in-memory encode / decode path is provided. Two carriers of §6.4 are
// provided, each a device worker speaking the §6.2 carrier contract: (:uart1), the UART1 header (TX
// GPIO35, RX GPIO36; board_pack pin_uart1_tx / pin_uart1_rx, window 12;
// board/apps/device_lib/device_esp32s3_uart1.silica; transport_esp32s3_wifi_plan.md stage 1,
// transport_links_design.md phase B, board plan item N), and (:usb_serial_jtag), the native USB-C jack
// through the USB-Serial-JTAG controller (window 7, 303A:1001 on the host, device role only;
// board/apps/device_lib/device_esp32s3_usb_serial_jtag.silica usb_serial_jtag_carrier;
// transport_esp32s3_wifi_plan.md §8 stage S-A). Their Carrier properties are the §6.4 rows: mtu 0,
// :stream, :reliable_ordered (compiler/stdlib/Carrier.silica answers them for the tags). UART0 is the
// console and is never a carrier (links design decision 17); the other §6.4 rows are not provided. The compiler consults provides_format today (sir_target_verify, E2410 for a derived
// encode / decode); provides_carrier is the row the links design's phase A check (E2412,
// provides_link beside it) reads when it lands, and the record of what this build ships until then.

export provides_format/1;
export provides_carrier/1;

fn provides_format(tag: string) -> boolean {
    case tag of {
        "etf" -> true;
        _: string -> false
    }
}

fn provides_carrier(tag: string) -> boolean {
    case tag of {
        "uart1" -> true;
        "usb_serial_jtag" -> true;
        _: string -> false
    }
}
